nss_core: read the memory counters without si_meminfo() in softirq

The DDR info the host sends a core is put together when the core's
first non-queue interrupt is handled, in the NAPI poll, i.e. in softirq
context: nss_core_handle_cause_nonqueue() -> nss_send_ddr_info() ->
nss_get_ddr_info() -> si_meminfo(). si_meminfo() counts the block
device buffers through nr_blockdev_pages(), which takes the superblock
inode list lock, and the rest of the kernel takes that lock with
softirqs enabled. Lockdep reports it ("inconsistent {SOFTIRQ-ON-W} ->
{IN-SOFTIRQ-W} usage", on IPQ5018 at every boot) and turns itself off;
if the softirq interrupted a holder of that lock on the same CPU, it
would deadlock.

Only the total, shared and free RAM go into the result and the log;
the buffer count was only logged. Read them from totalram_pages() and
the vmstat counters, which are fine in any context, and drop the
buffer count from the log line.

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
---
--- a/nss_core.c
+++ b/nss_core.c
@@ -561,13 +561,23 @@ static void nss_get_ddr_info(struct nss_mmu_ddr_info *mmu, char *name)
 {
 	__be32 avail_ddr;
 	long cached;
-	struct sysinfo vals;
+	unsigned long totalram, sharedram, freeram;
 	struct device_node *node;
 
-	si_meminfo(&vals);
+	/*
+	 * The first call comes from the NAPI poll of the core's first
+	 * non-queue interrupt (nss_send_ddr_info()), in softirq context.
+	 * si_meminfo() is not for that: its buffer count takes the
+	 * superblock inode list lock, which the rest of the kernel takes
+	 * with softirqs on. Read the plain counters instead; the buffer
+	 * count was only ever logged.
+	 */
+	totalram = totalram_pages();
+	sharedram = global_node_page_state(NR_SHMEM);
+	freeram = global_zone_page_state(NR_FREE_PAGES);
 	cached = global_node_page_state(NR_FILE_PAGES);
 
-	avail_ddr = (vals.totalram + cached + vals.sharedram) * vals.mem_unit;
+	avail_ddr = (totalram + cached + sharedram) * PAGE_SIZE;
 	mmu->num_active_cores = nss_top_main.num_nss;
 
 	/*
@@ -641,9 +651,8 @@ case3:
 	 */
 	mmu->start_address = 0;
 	mmu->ddr_size = (avail_ddr + (127 << 20)) & (~127 << 20);
-	nss_info_always("RAM pages fr %lu buf %lu cached %lu %lu : %lu %u\n",
-			vals.freeram, vals.bufferram, cached, vals.sharedram,
-			vals.totalram, mmu->ddr_size);
+	nss_info_always("RAM pages fr %lu cached %lu %lu : %lu %u\n",
+			freeram, cached, sharedram, totalram, mmu->ddr_size);
 }
 
 /*
